The portable C in the scenario setup-colors-own: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/setup-colors-own.txt,
see harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what
is expected in its place.
Deviation: 10 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the sample of the colours at the right of the screen is grey on black
on these screens, as what DOS has shown is. Its first four cells of the
second row are spaces, in front of Mode, and cover the end of the banner's
second line, which is longer in the portable C and reaches under the sample:
the rule of the name takes spaces in that colour for the screen behind the
banner, and the three cells where the line would have letters are the
sample's spaces

